      "words": 57563,
      "summary": {
        "text": "The Russian-language edition of the WHO operational handbook on tuberculosis, Module 1, on tuberculosis preventive treatment, extracted as a single block of the whole document. It opens with the ISBN, licence and disclaimer pages and a contents list covering acknowledgements, abbreviations, definitions and chapters on identifying target populations, excluding TB disease, testing for TB infection, treatment regimens and safety. Later chapters and annexes address programme management, monitoring and data collection tools, including tables of the preventive treatment cascade. It ends with a patient information leaflet explaining that shorter regimens of one to three months can prevent infection progressing to disease.",
        "status": "draft"
      },
